---
/**
 * Terms & Conditions. NOT ported — the prototype had no terms content at
 * all, just dead footer buttons. This is a from-scratch draft of standard
 * B2B terms matching how the product actually works (subscription software
 * + network services, manual payment marking, no consumer relationship).
 *
 * DRAFT — must be reviewed by counsel before launch. noindex until then.
 * Reuses the article (.art-*) styles rather than inventing a new layout.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '20 August 2026';
---

<Base title="Terms & Conditions" description="The terms governing use of Hyperporter's Autopilot software and Horizon network services." noindex>
  <div class="sec wrap">
    <div class="art-top">
      <div class="b-meta"><em>Legal</em><span>Last updated {updated}</span></div>
      <h1 class="art-title">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="art-dek">
        These terms govern your use of Hyperporter's services. They are a working draft pending legal review — if
        you have questions, contact <a href="mailto:hello@hyperporter.com">hello@hyperporter.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="art-body">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Hyperporter ("we", "us") provides travel operations infrastructure to travel businesses: <strong>Autopilot</strong>,
        subscription software that coordinates trip workflows, and <strong>Horizon</strong>, a network of vetted
        local ground operators through which we arrange trip services. Our registered office is Intelak Hub, Offices
        4, One Central, Dubai World Trade Center, Dubai, UAE.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Who these terms apply to</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are provided to businesses — travel agencies, advisors, creators, and destination management
        companies — not to consumers. By creating an account or engaging us, you confirm you are acting in the
        course of business and are authorised to bind the business you represent.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Autopilot (software)</h2>
      <p>
        Autopilot is provided on a monthly subscription. We grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use
        it for your own business operations during your subscription. You retain ownership of the data you put into
        it; we retain ownership of the software. Fees, plan limits, and any trial arrangements are as stated at the
        point of purchase.
      </p>
      <p>
        Automated steps in Autopilot can be placed under manual control at any time. <strong>Payment marking is
        always manual</strong>: the software does not move money or confirm receipt of funds on its own — a human
        confirms every payment.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Horizon (network services)</h2>
      <p>
        Where you engage us to run a trip through Horizon, we arrange services with local operators on the terms
        agreed per trip (itinerary, price, and inclusions as quoted). Quotes are valid as stated on the quote;
        availability is only assured once re-verified and confirmed. Operator services are subject to the operator's
        own conditions where these are notified to you in the quote.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep your account credentials secure and accurate.</li>
        <li>Ensure information you supply about trips and travellers is accurate and lawfully shared with us.</li>
        <li>Hold the licences and consents your own business requires to sell travel.</li>
        <li>Not misuse the services, attempt unauthorised access, or resell access without our agreement.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Neither party excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded. Otherwise, our aggregate liability in any
        twelve-month period is limited to the fees you paid us in that period, and neither party is liable for
        indirect or consequential loss. We are not the supplier of underlying travel services (transport,
        accommodation, activities); responsibility for their performance rests with the operator providing them,
        without limiting any responsibility we have for our own arranging services.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can cancel your subscription effective at the end of the current billing period. We may suspend or
        terminate for material breach, non-payment, or unlawful use, with notice where practicable. On termination
        we will make your data available for export for 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; material changes will be notified to account holders in advance. Continued use
        after the effective date constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Emirate of Dubai and the applicable federal laws of the United
        Arab Emirates, and the courts of Dubai have exclusive jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
